# with the average accuracy increase from the semantic methods, over the 15 model-dataset pairs of
# Table 3 (low-BLEU / highest-gain cells among them).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Negative result lowers through the null dual null_correlation(X, Y, S, Exp), conclusion
#     not_correlated(X, Y, S) with X = avg_bleu, Y = accuracy_increase, S = model_dataset_pairs --
#     a genuine negation of a correlation conclusion, so the null rule is the right target rather
#     than a positive conclusion over negative-content constants.
#   * Both mandatory corpus-v1 CQs are annotated unmet-gap, so no complete argument is declarable
#     and the claim lands `gap` (E2-style): significance <- CQ1 (Table 3 notes assert "no
#     correlation observed" but no test statistic / alpha appears; recomputed r = -0.234, t ~
#     -0.87 confirms the direction only); adequate_power <- CQ2 (n = 15 fixed, no power analysis,
#     so absence-is-informative is unbacked). No mandatory CQ met, so only the premise leaf is
#     kept. The optional BLEU-reference CQ is also unmet; optional, no status effect.
#   * The contrary pair correlated/not_correlated is symmetric in corpus-v1, but this unit
#     concludes only not_correlated over the (avg_bleu, accuracy_increase) pair; C05's positive
#     conclusion is over a different pair (avg_seq_length) in a separate unit, so no mutual rebut
#     edge is forced here (attack completeness is arg-conclusion-level). Recomputed r lives in nl.
#     Dead end N06 is corroboration-adjacent (its lesson parallels C06) but the attack vocabulary
#     correctly yields no edge; N07/N12 are unrelated rejected alternatives.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact semantic-self-consistency at sha256:970cd14ac108
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c06
  nl      = "Average BLEU score does not correlate with the average accuracy increase from the semantic methods over the 15 model-dataset pairs of Table 3 (recomputed Pearson r ~= -0.234, not significant at n = 15)"
  formal  = not_correlated(avg_bleu, accuracy_increase, model_dataset_pairs)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaf is present ... ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the Table 3 (BLEU, accuracy_increase) pairs and the asserted no-correlation
# note, folded into refs (including the low-BLEU / highest-gain counter-cell).
leaf e1 : reports(e04, correlation(avg_bleu, accuracy_increase, model_dataset_pairs, absent))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C06, evidence/tables/table3_sequence_length_bleu.md, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: significance_reported(e04) and powered(e04) have no honest leaves -- no
# test/alpha is reported and there is no power analysis at n = 15 -- and corpus-v1 makes both
# mandatory for the null dual. The claim's complete-support set is empty.)

status c06

